I provide affordable SEO consultancy by agreeing a focused scope around the work your business needs. You work directly with me on research, priorities and implementation. The quote sets out the deliverables and what is excluded before work starts.

A low fee alone does not tell you whether an SEO service is useful. Compare the work included, the evidence behind the recommendations and your team's capacity to act on them.

## What affordable SEO includes

Affordable SEO means a defined budget with clear priorities and deliverables. A smaller budget may support a focused audit or a limited implementation scope. It should not come with a promise of complete SEO coverage or guaranteed rankings.

I quote for the work I can deliver directly. Agency fees vary with scope, staffing and service level. I do not infer the quality of another provider's work from its price or claim an equivalent agency package without comparing the deliverables.

You discuss the site with the person carrying out the work. I prioritise the investigations and changes that have a clear relationship to your business goals. Rankings and revenue remain outcomes to measure rather than promises attached to each billed hour.

## How to compare consultant and agency fees

An independent consultant and an agency can have different staffing and delivery models. Their fees need to be compared against the actual scope. There is no reliable universal split showing how much of an agency retainer pays for SEO work, overhead or profit.

My [SEO consulting practice](/services/seo-consulting/) provides direct access to the specialist doing the work. Compare my proposal with an agency proposal using the included tasks, delivery capacity and reporting expectations. I cannot infer another provider's hours or overheads from its quoted fee.

My [freelance SEO consultancy](/services/freelance-seo-consultant/) is suited to businesses that want direct access to the specialist. An agency may be a better fit when a project requires a larger team or several disciplines at once.

## What's included at affordable rates

The agreed scope may include the following work. A one-off audit and an ongoing retainer have different deliverables:

- **Technical SEO audit**: A thorough [technical SEO audit](/services/technical-seo-audit/) covering crawlability, indexation, Core Web Vitals, schema markup, and site architecture. This forms the foundation of every campaign.
- **Keyword and competitor research**: Proper data-driven research using professional tools, not guesswork. I identify the terms that will actually drive revenue, not just traffic.
- **Content strategy**: A clear roadmap of what content to create, update, or consolidate, built around search intent and topical authority.
- **On-page optimisation**: Title tags, meta descriptions, internal linking, heading structure, and content improvements across priority pages.
- **Monthly reporting**: Transparent reporting showing what was done, what changed, and what's next. No vanity metrics: just the numbers that matter to your business.
- **Direct communication**: You talk to me, not an account handler. Questions get answered quickly, and strategy adjustments happen without layers of approval.

The scope scales with your budget, but the quality of thinking and execution stays the same regardless of what you're paying. I'd rather do fewer things brilliantly than spread myself thin across tasks that won't move the needle.

## Warning signs of cheap SEO

Assess an SEO proposal through the work and evidence it provides. A low price is not proof of poor practice. Ask these questions before accepting any complete SEO package:

- **Link schemes**: Ask how links will be obtained. Links intended to manipulate rankings can violate Google's spam policies. A low price does not itself establish that a provider uses them.
- **Unreviewed content**: Ask who checks accuracy, evidence and originality. Content needs to help the reader regardless of whether AI was used to draft it.
- **Guaranteed rankings**: A provider cannot control Google's results. Ask for an implementation plan and realistic measurement instead of a promised position or deadline.
- **No transparency**: If your provider can't explain exactly what they're doing and why, that's a serious red flag. A provider should explain the work and its limits regardless of the fee.

Ask for an explanation of each recommended fix and the evidence that supports it. A tool's link-risk score alone is not a reason to disavow backlinks. My guide to [how much SEO costs](/services/how-much-does-seo-cost/) explains different engagement types and the scope to compare.

## How I keep costs down without cutting quality

My approach to keeping SEO affordable is straightforward: I invest in efficiency, not headcount.

I use professional-grade tools, including Ahrefs, Google Search Console, Screaming Frog, and custom scripts, to automate the data gathering and analysis that would otherwise take hours of manual work. That means more of your budget goes toward strategic thinking and implementation rather than routine tasks.

I also prioritise ruthlessly. Rather than producing a 40-page audit document that overwhelms you with issues, I identify the changes that will have the biggest impact on your rankings and revenue, and we tackle those first. This focused approach aims to put the available budget into the most useful work first. The results and total cost still depend on the agreed scope and implementation.

I work remotely, keep my client roster deliberately small, and handle everything myself. No subcontracting to overseas teams, no passing your work to a junior. The person you speak to is the person doing the work, and that person has years of experience across technical SEO, content strategy, and organic growth.

## Pricing transparency

I believe you should know what you're paying before we start. I offer flexible arrangements to suit different budgets:

- **Technical SEO audit (£495)**: A defined one-off investigation and prioritised action plan. The [technical audit page](/services/technical-seo-audit/) specifies the site limit, delivery conditions and 60-minute walkthrough. Implementation is separate.
- **Monthly retainers**: Ongoing strategy, implementation and optimisation quoted around your agreed scope. The proposal states the fee and delivery priorities.
- **Project-based work**: Defined scope, defined cost. Site migrations, content overhauls, or technical fixes with a clear brief and timeline.

Every engagement starts with a free 20-minute SEO diagnosis focused on your biggest problem and the most useful next step, including whether you need ongoing support at all. I'd rather earn your trust than your money.

## How we work together

The process is simple and designed to respect your time:

1. **Free 20-minute SEO diagnosis**: We focus on your biggest search problem, your goals and what a realistic next step looks like.
2. **Proposal**: A clear proposal outlining the work, exclusions, fee and how results will be measured.
3. **Execution**: I get to work. You get regular updates and can reach me directly whenever you need to.
4. **Review and refine**: SEO is iterative. We review performance monthly and adjust strategy based on real data.

No long-term contracts, no lock-in periods. I keep clients because the work delivers value, not because they're trapped in a 12-month agreement.

